<div class="lead" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">
  There are two ways to start. If you're comfortable with the command line, three short commands will get you a working site you can poke around in. If you'd rather not touch a terminal, the second section is for you.
</div>

<section class="section-sm">
  <h2 class="h3">Before you begin</h2>
  <div class="card" style="margin-top: var(--space-lg);">
    <div class="card__eyebrow">You'll need</div>
    <div class="card__title">Three things, all free</div>
    <ul class="card__list">
      <li>Node.js 18 or later (<a href="https://nodejs.org">nodejs.org</a>) — this is the tool that turns the source files into a website</li>
      <li>A free GitHub account (<a href="https://github.com">github.com</a>) — this is where your site's source lives online</li>
      <li>A terminal — any Mac, Linux, or Windows machine has one</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<ol class="guide-steps">
  <li class="guide-step">
    <h2 class="guide-step__title">Download a copy</h2>
    <div class="guide-step__body">
      <p>Pick any folder name that fits your project.</p>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/{{ meta.githubOwner }}/{{ meta.githubRepo }}.git my-publication
cd my-publication</code></pre>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="guide-step">
    <h2 class="guide-step__title">Install what it needs</h2>
    <div class="guide-step__body">
      <pre><code>npm install</code></pre>
      <p>Takes under a minute on a modern connection.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="guide-step">
    <h2 class="guide-step__title">Open it in your browser</h2>
    <div class="guide-step__body">
      <pre><code>npm start</code></pre>
      <p>The site is now running at <code>http://localhost:8080</code>. Open it, click around, try the reading tools, see how it feels. Any change you save to a file shows up in the browser within about a second.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
</ol>

<div class="callout" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">
  <div class="callout__title">Prefer not to use the terminal?</div>
  <p>You can set things up entirely through a browser. Make a copy of the project on GitHub, connect it to a free host like Cloudflare Pages, and use the built-in browser editor to write. No command line needed. <a href="/docs/getting-started/no-terminal/">Here's the walk-through.</a></p>
</div>

